      advanced: "Defaults verified from `fastp --help` (0.23.2 and 0.23.4): --qualified_quality_phred 15, --unqualified_percent_limit 40, --n_base_limit 5, --length_required 15, --length_limit 0 (off), --average_qual 0 (off), --complexity_threshold 30 with --low_complexity_filter off, --trim_front1/--trim_tail1/--max_len1 0. fastp accepts 0–30 for front trims and 0–100 for tail trims. Read-2 trims follow read 1 unless given; ARVA always writes them out for pairs. --length_limit is checked after trimming (filter.cpp) and is turned off by --disable_length_filtering.",
