      why: "A read of length L contains only L − k + 1 k-mers, so a base is covered by fewer k-mers than reads; k-mer coverage is therefore lower than read depth, and the difference grows with k. Comparing it with Flye's read depth or with the depth in the read statistics would mislead.",
